(4298691, 616757, 51538, '<td valign="top">When one camera is not enough.  Nice idea.  I have been playing with my Epson 1640XL scanner (11 x 17") recently.  When people complain about dust bunnies on their Canon sensors, they should try cleaning a 11 x 17" sensor!  At 600dpi scans it''s virtually impossible to rid the scanning glass of minuscule particles.  The point was that merging various tools, analog and digital often creates useful effects - like you have done with this photo.</td>', 'When one camera is not enough.  Nice idea.  I have been playing with my Epson 1640XL scanner (11 x 17") recently.  When people complain about dust bunnies on their Canon sensors, they should try cleaning a 11 x 17" sensor!  At 600dpi scans it''s virtually impossible to rid the scanning glass of minuscule particles.  The point was that merging various tools, analog and digital often creates useful effects - like you have done with this photo.', '2007-12-07 10:19:28.000000', NULL, 0),
